WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
Imagine3D-LLM: Teaching MLLMs to imagine 3D scenes before answering. A coarse Gaussian reconstruction of a room appears behind the title.

00:04.000 --> 00:09.000
Multi-view images show the same room from different viewpoints. Image patches become 6,720 image tokens from 32 views.

00:09.000 --> 00:16.000
A standard multimodal LLM concatenates image and question tokens, then processes the sequence through its 28 layers to answer.

00:16.000 --> 00:25.000
Imagine3D-LLM introduces Gaussian summary tokens between the image tokens and the question. Their layer-14 hidden states can be decoded into a coarse 3D scene.

00:25.000 --> 00:31.000
Inside layers 1 to 14, 2,592 summary tokens form a deliberate bottleneck for 6,720 image tokens.

00:31.000 --> 00:41.000
Summary tokens attend across views and gather shared evidence. With too few slots to copy every patch, they consolidate recurring scene features.

00:41.000 --> 00:49.000
At layer 14, summary tokens decode into 3D Gaussians. The imagined scene is rendered at the input viewpoints and compared with the real images using reconstruction loss.

00:49.000 --> 00:59.000
The reconstruction signal flows back through the earlier layers and improves image features. Across views, the same objects develop more consistent representations.

00:59.000 --> 01:05.000
The remaining LLM layers use the improved image features and Gaussian summary tokens to answer the question.

01:05.000 --> 01:17.000
Benchmark charts compare Imagine3D-LLM with other models on SPAR, SQA3D and Real-3DQA, showing improved spatial reasoning.

01:17.000 --> 01:20.500
Imagine3D-LLM. Imagine the scene before answering. The coarse Gaussian room reconstruction returns behind the closing title.
